# Findings — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

**Read at the start of every session.** This is the project's working memory:
what is known, what was tried and failed, and what was believed and then
withdrawn.

{{IF FINDINGS_CAP}}**HARD CAP: {{FINDINGS_CAP}} lines**, checked by
`{{RECORDS_HELPER}} lint`. Not a guideline. When a new entry would push the file
over, something must be retired or promoted to a doc *in the same edit*.

{{ENDIF}}**One finding per entry, a pointer and not prose.** A findings file too
expensive to load is one nobody reads, and an unread one grows without limit —
which is how it becomes unreadable. That constraint holds whether or not a line
cap is enforcing it. `{{RECORDS_HELPER}} lint` checks the part a cap never
could: that every entry is actually **sourced**.

This is **not** a progress log, a changelog, or a session journal. Sessions go in
`{{SESSIONS_FILE}}`.

## Format — one finding per entry, and keep it to a few lines

```
<status> YYYY-MM-DD [`<sha>`]({{FORGE_URL}}/commit/<sha>) The finding, stated as a
  claim, in one or two sentences. → doc/<file>.md §<n>
```

- **status** — `✓` holds · `⚠` partial or unsettled · `✗` withdrawn
- **sha** — the commit that establishes or fixes it, linked. No commit, no entry:
  a finding with nothing to point at is an opinion.
- **→** — where the evidence lives. Anything needing more than two sentences goes
  into a doc and is referenced from here. **Nothing bulky in this file.**

## What earns an entry

Only the **non-obvious, surprising, or hard-won**:

- a result that contradicted an assumption going in
- an approach tried and ruled out, with *why* it failed
- a constraint discovered the hard way
- a number that will be quoted later — with the conditions it was measured under

Not routine progress, not anything obvious from the diff, not "implemented X as
planned." When in doubt, leave it out.

## Withdrawn entries stay

Mark them `✗` and strike the claim — do not delete it. An entry that turned out
wrong is the cheapest protection against taking the same wrong turn twice, and
deleting it destroys exactly that. A withdrawn entry earns its line.

Retire an entry outright only once it has become uncontroversial background that
no future session would act on differently.

